Jitendra: It's been hours.
Sira: ...
Jitendra: You should rest.
Jitendra: The sun is about to rise.
Sira: ...
Jitendra: Sira.
Sira: ...
Jitendra: Sira. [pause=1] You can't do this to yourself.
Jitendra: None of us could've predicted this.
Jitendra: Not even the Balian Bawi saw it coming and she predicted every disaster that happened to us before.
Jitendra: Stop blaming yourself.
Sira: And how would you know that, Jitendra?
Sira: Did the spirits tell you that directly?
Sira: Look around you! Everything is burning!
Sira: How am I not gonna blame myself?!
Jitendra: It's exactly because the spirits didn't tell us anything that we can't let one person shoulder all the blame, Sira!
Jitendra: Especially you.
Jitendra: You've done nothing but sacrificed your entire life for this village and forest.
Jitendra: Why should they punish you?
Sira: ...
